From 9860c4b0b4d9d7cd94bf84842cbb306c9e96314a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:07:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Longer exposures in low light, proportional AGC,
 faster AF

Agc:
- with a sensor VBLANK control, the frame is lengthened for long
  exposures (one more line of blanking allows one more line of
  exposure), up to maxFrameDuration (tuning, default 100 ms); the simple
  pipeline handles VBLANK in its delayed controls, written first;
- the total exposure (lines x gain) is split as exposure time up to the
  mode's frame, gain up to gainThreshold (default 4x), longer frames,
  then the rest of the gain range;
- proportional correction (ratio to the target mean sample value, square
  root close to it, 0.5x to 2x per step) instead of 10 % steps.

Af:
- the coarse pass stops once the measure has fallen below peakDrop
  (0.7) of the best for peakDropSteps (2) steps;
- the fine pass covers +-fineRange (half a coarse step) on a grid
  centred on the coarse peak;
- the lens range can be limited (rangeMin, rangeMax);
- continuous mode rescans after a 50 % change for 8 measures (was 35 %
  for 6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
